      "before": "<p style=\"margin-top:0;\">Let $k(x,x')=x^\\top x'$ on $D=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^d:\\|x\\|\\le1\\}$ with noise variance $\\lambda$. Show that $\\gamma_T\\le\\frac d2\\log\\big(1+\\frac{T}{\\lambda d}\\big)=O(d\\log T)$, exhibit a design that attains it when $d$ divides $T$, and show that it cannot be attained when $T\\lt d$.</p>",
      "after": "<p style=\"margin-top:0;\">Let $d\\ge1$ and $T\\ge1$ be integers, and let $k(x,x')=x^\\top x'$ on $D=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^d:\\|x\\|\\le1\\}$ with noise variance $\\lambda$. Show that $\\gamma_T\\le\\frac d2\\log\\big(1+\\frac{T}{\\lambda d}\\big)=O(d\\log T)$, exhibit a design that attains it when $d$ divides $T$, and show that it cannot be attained when $T\\lt d$.</p>",
      "count": 1,
